    index: 12,
    part: "PART 4 — LAUNCH",
    title: "Rollout Sequencing",
    subtitle: "What Order to Add These In",
    free: false,
    bodyHtml:
      "<p>Don't run all eight junctures at once. This is the single most common way agencies waste the budget from Chapter 2 — not by picking the wrong tools, but by adding all of them in the same month and never properly piloting any one of them. That's the rollout pattern behind the 50-70% three-month churn number from Chapter 0.</p><div class=\"steps\"><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"circle\">1</div><div class=\"body\"><b>Core ATS/CRM first if you're on spreadsheets.</b><span>Every other juncture below either writes into this system or reads from it. Get it wrong first and you're migrating twice.</span></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"circle\">2</div><div class=\"body\"><b>Sourcing next.</b><span>The highest time-cost juncture per Chapter 1 — the fastest way to free up recruiter hours for everything else on this list.</span></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"circle\">3</div><div class=\"body\"><b>Interview intelligence.</b><span>The easiest win in the guide (Chapter 7). Free to trial, minimal workflow change, builds momentum before you tackle a harder juncture.</span></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"circle\">4</div><div class=\"body\"><b>Business development.</b><span>Start the 2-week manual pilot from Chapter 4 in parallel with everything above — it costs nothing and takes time to show a signal.</span></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"circle\">5</div><div class=\"body\"><b>Reference checking.</b><span>Lower urgency than sourcing or screening, but the highest cost-of-delay per candidate once you're closing more roles.</span></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"circle\">6</div><div class=\"body\"><b>Screening, rediscovery, account management.</b><span>Add these once the first five are running cleanly, not before. They compound the value of everything above rather than standing alone.</span></div></div></div><h3>A Realistic Timeline</h3><table><tr><th>Month</th><th>Focus</th></tr><tr><td>Month 1</td><td>ATS/CRM migration (if needed) and sourcing pilot</td></tr><tr><td>Month 2</td><td>Interview intelligence live; business development pilot running in parallel</td></tr><tr><td>Month 3</td><td>Reference checking added; review Chapter 16 KPIs on everything shipped so far</td></tr><tr><td>Month 4+</td><td>Screening, rediscovery, and account management, one at a time, only where Month 1-3 data shows a real gap</td></tr></table><div class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"head\">If you're already on spreadsheets and mid-quarter</div><p>Don't wait for a clean calendar boundary to start. The ATS/CRM migration in step 1 takes real time regardless of when you begin it — starting a month late costs you a month of everything downstream.</p></div>",
